From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] cs_playsound: report that mri_play_sound is unsupported on Windows

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: mri_play_sound() fork()s and the
child writes a temporary .au file, runs the player through
system("tcsh -c '...'"), sleeps and removes the file. The child keeps running
AFNI code without exec, which Windows cannot do, and the layer deliberately
does not declare fork(). The file is part of libmri, so it must compile. On
Windows the function now prints an error and returns without playing
anything; users are 1dsound (optional program) and the AFNI GUI (out of
scope).

diff --git a/src/cs_playsound.c b/src/cs_playsound.c
index 27327a2..e68c4e0 100644
--- a/src/cs_playsound.c
+++ b/src/cs_playsound.c
@@ -160,6 +160,14 @@ void mri_play_sound_rate_fac( float fff ){
 /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /* Play sound from a 1D image (up to 4 columns) */
 
+#ifdef _WIN32  /* afni-win: fork() does not exist on Windows */
+void mri_play_sound( MRI_IMAGE *imin , int ignore )
+{
+   (void)imin ; (void)ignore ;
+   ERROR_message("mri_play_sound: playing sound is not supported on Windows") ;
+   return ;
+}
+#else
 void mri_play_sound( MRI_IMAGE *imin , int ignore )
 {
    MRI_IMAGE *qim ;
@@ -220,6 +228,7 @@ void mri_play_sound( MRI_IMAGE *imin , int ignore )
    unlink(fname) ;
    _exit(0) ;
 }
+#endif /* _WIN32 */
 
 /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /*-------- convert value in range -1..1 into 8 bit code via 'mu-law' --------*/
